# Showcase Scenario

Customer demo scenario with a Naemon backend, showcasing custom
action menus.

## Start

    %> make prepare

Thruk is available at `http://127.0.0.4:60080/demo/thruk/` (user `omdadmin`, password `omd`).

## Demo: Action Menus

Open the details page of the `Sticky Logfile` service (host `localhost`):

    http://127.0.0.4:60080/demo/thruk/cgi-bin/extinfo.cgi?type=2&host=localhost&service=Sticky%20Logfile

The service is CRITICAL out of the box and shows two custom action menu icons:

* **Restart Service** (redo icon): triggers a server action which restarts the
  grafana service of the demo site. A confirmation dialog is shown before the
  action runs and the script output is displayed as user feedback.

* **Showcase Menu** (dropdown icon):
  * **Service Note** - a form based action menu. Enter a note and press save,
    the note is send as server action to `add_note.sh` and saved to
    `var/thruk/showcase_notes.log` inside the container.
  * **Open Grafana** - a simple link menu item.
  * **Trigger Sticky Logfile Check** - (re-)creates the sticky logfile problem
    of the `Sticky Logfile` service, to demo the full problem lifecycle.
  * **Reset Sticky Logfile Check** - resets the sticky logfile check of the
    `Sticky Logfile` service, to demo a problem which can only be resolved by
    a custom action.
  * **Trigger Sticky Logfile Check** - creates the sticky logfile problem
    again, so the demo can be repeated.
  * **Failing Action** - a server action which always fails, to demo the error
    handling of action menus.

The menus are applied by the `action_menu_apply` rules in
`/omd/sites/demo/etc/thruk/thruk_local.d/showcase.conf`, the server actions
are defined in the `action_menu_actions` section of the same file and the
menus themselves live in `/omd/sites/demo/etc/thruk/action_menus/`:

* `showcase_menu.json` - a static json menu.
* `showcase_js_menu.js` - a javascript based menu (applied to all hosts,
  visible on the host details page) with a dynamic submenu which lists all
  services of the host by querying the rest api.

## Test

    %> make test
